<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kidarite Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">320 CE – 477 CE (approx.) · capital Balkh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first of the Hunnic dynasties to rule Bactria and Gandhara, named after its founder Kidara and long locked in war with Sasanian Persia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kidarites emerged in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Bactria</a> in the 4th century, probably from among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chionites">Chionites</a> who invaded the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kushano-sasanian-kingdom">Kushano-Sasanian Kingdom</a>. Their eponymous leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kidara">Kidara</a> issued coins in the Kushan style and claimed the old Kushan title, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a> and later spreading into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gandhara">Gandhara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They governed a mixed population of Bactrians and Indians, issuing gold coins modelled on Kushan and Sasanian types, some with Brahmi legends naming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kidara">Kidara</a>. They fought repeated wars with Sasanian kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a>, and probably clashed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 467 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> drove them from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Bactria</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hephthalite-empire">Hephthalite Empire</a> soon took over their northern lands. Remnant Kidarite principalities held out in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gandhara">Gandhara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> until the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alchon-huns">Alchon Huns</a> absorbed them in the late 5th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kidarite-kingdom.jpg" alt="Kidarite Kingdom" width="320" height="360"><figcaption>Image: Alx bio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kidarite_Tamga.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>320 CE – 477 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Balkh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kidara I, Kunkhas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Zoroastrianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bactrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kidarites, Kidara Huns</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=398&amp;focus=kidarite-kingdom" aria-label="Kidarite Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6359 853 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kidarite Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6679 1109L6757 1168M6679 1109L6679 1109M6679 1109L6357 1235M6679 1109L6729 1110M6679 1109L6757 1183"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6757 1168h0M6679 1109h0M6357 1235h0M6729 1110h0M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6679 1109h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6679 1109h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Balkh. <a href="/atlas?year=398&amp;focus=kidarite-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
